[Mod] Topographic Map 1.5.0 – new title bar buttons and 9 new looks

The [b]Topography[/b] layer tints land by height and the sea by depth on the tactical map, with hill shading, contour lines and chart-style depth lines – for low-level flying, terrain masking, and knowing where your submarine has room to dive. All heights and depths are the game's own terrain data, what the simulation uses.

1.5.0 tidies up the buttons and reworks the list of looks.

[b]New in 1.5.0[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Title bar buttons[/b] are now one small group of icons instead of four wide text buttons: a mountain (Topography on/off), the current look's colours (opens the list of looks), a list (Legend) and a crosshair (cursor height on/off). Hover for the name; a lit one has an orange icon
[*][b]9 new looks[/b] – day: Soviet General Staff map, Bathymetric chart, Desert storm, Satellite, 1940s chart; night: Recon photo, Survey sonar (depth as a multibeam rainbow), White phosphor, Amber display
[*][b]8 looks removed[/b] (Atlas, Paper sea chart, Parchment, Quiet, Atlas dusk, ECDIS dusk, Thermal imager, Neon) – 19 looks in all now. If you used one, the map goes back to Standard by day and Midnight at night
[*]A few looks toned down: quieter lines in Phosphor green, calmer water in Glacier, dark grey lowland in Black
[/list]

[b]Still in[/b]
[list]
[*]Height or depth under the cursor, in m and ft
[*]Select an aircraft: terrain at or above its altitude is hatched red, and the readout gives the clearance
[*]Select a submarine: where it is below the thermal layer, where the layer ends, water too shallow for it, and the water under the keel
[*]Your own looks as small theme files: save any look, change the colours, and the map follows when you save
[*]The layer in the mission editor too
[/list]

[b]Which game version?[/b] One Workshop item for both: a build for 0.8.7 (flat map) and one for the 3D globe map, and the right one switches on by itself. 1.5.0 was run in the game on 0.8.7. [b]On the beta right now[/b], Anchor Chain itself doesn't start yet ([url=https://github.com/seapower-modders/AnchorChain/issues/19]Anchor Chain issue #19[/url]), so no Anchor Chain mod loads there until it's updated.

Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3380210757]Anchor Chain[/url].

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3826122523]Workshop page[/url] · [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerTopo]Source code (MIT)[/url]

